Resolve precompiled OS dependencies from a local directory instead of GitHub.

Bundlex fetches precompiled native libraries (ffmpeg, opus, srt, ...) with
`Req.get!` during `mix deps.compile`. Under Bazel that is a network fetch inside
a build action: it is not covered by the action key, it needs egress the RBE
executors should not rely on, and each consuming plugin downloads and embeds its
own copy -- five separate 70.8 MB libavcodec.so copies in one release.

Every one of those archives is already a pinned `http_file` in //MODULE.bazel
(@membrane_precompiled_*), staged by //build:mix_app.bzl into
BUNDLEX_LOCAL_PRECOMPILED_DIR. When a file matching the URL's basename is
present there, copy it; otherwise fall back to the original download so this
stays a no-op outside Bazel.

//build:mix_release.bzl applied the same change by rewriting the source in
deps/. That worked because mix_release compiled bundlex itself; mix_app receives
bundlex already compiled, so the fix has to live at the repository instead.

--- a/lib/bundlex/toolchain/common/unix/os_deps.ex
+++ b/lib/bundlex/toolchain/common/unix/os_deps.ex
@@ -246,6 +246,16 @@
     end
   end

   defp download(url, dest) do
+    local = System.get_env("BUNDLEX_LOCAL_PRECOMPILED_DIR")
+
+    if local && File.exists?(Path.join(local, Path.basename(url))) do
+      File.cp!(Path.join(local, Path.basename(url)), dest)
+    else
+      download_remote(url, dest)
+    end
+  end
+
+  defp download_remote(url, dest) do
     response = Req.get!(url)

